  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trust Fund for Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative Implementation Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;This trust fund will provide financial support to countries seeking to  implement or considering implementation of, the EITI Principles and  Criteria and to generally improve extractive industries governance and  transparency in countries and through country, regional and global  activities.
 
 For legislative reasons, the USA is not able to join the existing MDTF  for EITI Implementation Support (TF053509). Therefore, the USAID SDTF  and the MDTF will be operationally equivalent, and both trust funds  together will constitute a trust fund facility under common  governance.
 
 EITI is an existing legal entity. The TFs under the EITI Facility are  independent from EITI in terms of governance and implementation. There  is nonetheless a cooperative relationship with EITI as clearly laid  out in the Memorandum of Understanding (attached in section 5.9).  The  EITI Facility is intended to provide EITI implementation support  through country, regional and global activities consistent with the  principles articulated in the Statement of Principles and Agreed  Actions adopted at the first plenary conference in London in June 2003  and the criteria articulated in the Statement of Outcomes adopted at  the second plenary conference in London in March 2005 (the EITI  Principles and Criteria) by the partnership that has now become the  EITI. The TF funds will be used to develop, broaden and increase  transparency over payments and revenues in the extractive sectors in  countries needing these resources.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
